## Design notes

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **Missing file** | `ENOENT` caught → defaults returned, reason `'missing'` |
| **Permission errors, etc.** | Other read errors → defaults, reason `'unreadable'` |
| **Malformed JSON** | `JSON.parse` error caught → reason `'invalid-json'` |
| **Valid JSON but wrong type** (e.g. `[]`, `"hi"`, `null`) | Rejected → reason `'invalid-shape'` |
| **Partial configs** | Deep-merged over defaults so missing keys get filled in |
| **Mutation safety** | `structuredClone` ensures callers can't accidentally mutate your `DEFAULTS` object |
| **BOM characters** | Stripped (common when files are saved by Windows editors) |
| **Silent failures** | Optional `onError` callback lets you log without forcing it |

`structuredClone` requires Node 17+. For older versions, use `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(defaults))`. If you need stricter validation (types, required fields), consider layering a schema validator like [Zod](https://zod.dev) or [Ajv](https://ajv.js.org) on top of the parsed result.

