| Empty file | Explicit `trim()` check throws → returns defaults |
| Malformed JSON | `JSON.parse` throws `SyntaxError` → returns defaults |
| Valid JSON but wrong shape (e.g. `[1,2,3]`, `null`, `"string"`) | Explicit type check throws → returns defaults |
| `defaults` mutated by caller | Returned via spread `{ ...defaults }` so caller can't accidentally mutate the source |

